    },
    {
     "_key": "00000000000c",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000002",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "In the heart of "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000004",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000003"
       ],
       "text": "Egypt’s"
      },
      {
       "_key": "e5zi8ic4i2x6",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " timeless landscape, where the fertile and meticulously irrigated sugar-cane fields sprawl, lies the ancient town of Kom Ombo. Tucked away 65 kilometers to the south of "
      },
      {
       "_key": "hssohpq88fyw",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "c8e8kvcgta52"
       ],
       "text": "Edfu"
      },
      {
       "_key": "7b59684fa1xz",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": ", this picturesque haven not only nurtures the original community of fellaheen, humble peasant farmers deeply rooted in their ancestral soil, but also extends its embrace to a thriving population of Nubians, forced from their homelands by the majestic creation of "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000007",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000006"
       ],
       "text": "Lake Nasser"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000008",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": ". Kom Ombo, with its serene beauty and historical significance, stands as a charming oasis easily accessible to those journeying between the captivating "
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000000a",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000009"
       ],
       "text": "cities of Aswan and Luxor"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000000b",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000003",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
